      "caption": "On NUMA machines each node has local RAM; remote accesses cross an interconnect and are slower.",
      "narration": "On a NUMA machine each node has its own memory. Touching another node's RAM crosses the interconnect and costs more latency.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Local vs remote memory",
